\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3566\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2783\"\n        ],\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Chat webview DOM additions: a sibling icon-only button #insrc-scratch (class attachbtn, inline SVG, title=\\\"scratchpads\\\") directly next to #insrc-attach (:2796); a dropdown #insrc-scratchmenu reusing the .popup.chatmenu / .item pattern of #insrc-histmenu (:2766, opens upward :2289, rows :2296) whose items are recent entries + \\\"New scratchpad\\\" + \\\"Browse all\\\"; one bootstrap listener (:2465-2486 pattern) posting 'scratch-open-menu'; the host 'insert-into-input' handler inserts text into #insrc-prompt (:2783) and focuses it. Attach flow (.attachbar :2787, 'pick-attachments' :3566) untouched.\",\n        \"entity\": \"Chat status-bar UI: scratchpad button + popup menu + input insertion\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:162\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/panels/types.ts\"\n        ],\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Two new webview viewTypes through the existing injected PanelFactory: 'insrc.scratchpads' (browse-all tabular editor-pane view: columns Name and Modified, per-row icon-only Open/Delete buttons with title hover text and data-id) and 'insrc.scratchpad' (single-document view rendering scratch content via textContent only, with the selectionchange → floating icon-only \\\"Send to chat\\\" button). Both keep the shared CSP+nonce shell and create-or-reveal single-instance lifecycle.\",\n        \"entity\": \"Scratchpad webview panel viewTypes\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"listScratches returns [] — the menu shows only \\\"New scratchpad\\\" + \\\"Browse all\\\", and Browse all shows an empty table with a hint row\",\n          \"input\": \"No ~/.insrc/scratches directory exists yet (fresh install) — readdir ENOENT\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"File name gets a -2 (then -3, ...) suffix and the entry is created without error\",\n          \"input\": \"Two scratchpads created within the same second from the same title (yyyymmdd-hhmmss-slug collision)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"createScratch slugifies the title (lowercase, spaces to dashes, non [a-z0-9-] dropped) so the generated id always matches ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$; an all-symbol title falls back to 'scratch'\",\n          \"input\": \"Title containing unicode, spaces, slashes or other non-slug characters\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"The entry is skipped from the list (not a crash); an entry whose stat fails is dropped rather than failing the whole list\",\n          \"input\": \"A file in ~/.insrc/scratches disappears between readdir and stat\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"Non-.md files in the scratches dir are ignored by listScratches; the temp file from an interrupted write is ignored (its name does not end in .md)\",\n          \"input\": \"Directory contains unrelated files (e.g. .DS_Store, a leftover .tmp)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"send-to-chat is accepted up to 64 KiB; larger selections are truncated at 64 KiB with a trailing ellipsis and still inserted\",\n          \"input\": \"User selects more than 64 KiB of text in the scratchpad document view\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"readScratch/deleteScratch refuse before touching the filesystem (ScratchRefused); the host handler logs and ignores the message\",\n          \"input\": \"A webview-to-host scratch-open/scratch-delete payload carries an id with path separators or shell metacharacters (../, ;, spaces)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"Deleting an already-deleted id resolves successfully; the browse table just re-renders without the row\",\n          \"input\": \"User double-clicks Delete on the same browse-table row\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"The document panel closes (or shows an empty state) and the entry disappears from the browse table on next refresh\",\n          \"input\": \"The scratchpad file backing an open insrc.scratchpad document view is deleted (from the browse table or the filesystem)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"insert-into-input appends at the end of the existing prompt text (with a separating newline when the input is non-empty) and focuses #insrc-prompt; the turn is NOT sent\",\n          \"input\": \"Chat input #insrc-prompt already contains unsent text when insert-into-input arrives\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"expected\": \"The floating button stays hidden; nothing is posted\",\n          \"input\": \"User clicks into the document without selecting any text (collapsed selection) and selectionchange fires\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"detection\": \"fs.mkdir/readdir/writeFile rejects with code EACCES, ENOSPC, EROFS, or the root is not a directory\",\n          \"recoverable\": true,\n          \"response\": \"createScratchStore/list/create surface ScratchStoreError; the host handler catches, logs via panelLog and shows a menu row 'scratchpads unavailable: <reason>'; menu still offers Browse all, which shows an error row\",\n          \"scenario\": \"~/.insrc/scratches cannot be created or written (read-only home, disk full, permissions)\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Scratchpads cannot be listed/created; the attach flow and chat itself keep working (failure is contained to the scratch features)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"detection\": \"id fails the ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ check before any fs call\",\n          \"recoverable\": true,\n          \"response\": \"readScratch/deleteScratch throw ScratchRefused; host logs and ignores the message — no filesystem access happens\",\n          \"scenario\": \"Malicious or malformed id in a webview message (path traversal ../, separators, metacharacters)\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"No impact; the attempt is refused and logged\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"detection\": \"readFile on the id rejects with ENOENT\",\n          \"recoverable\": true,\n          \"response\": \"readScratch maps ENOENT to ScratchNotFound; host closes the document panel (if open) and refreshes the browse table so the stale row disappears\",\n          \"scenario\": \"Opening or deleting a scratchpad whose file was deleted out-of-band while the menu/table was showing\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Stale menu/table row resolves on next interaction; no crash\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"detection\": \"writeFile of the temp file or the rename fails mid-create\",\n          \"recoverable\": true,\n          \"response\": \"ScratchStoreError surfaces to the host; the temp file is best-effort removed; no partial .md file is left visible (temp name does not match the *.md listing filter)\",\n          \"scenario\": \"Crash or EACCES/ENOSPC between temp write and rename during createScratch\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"No scratchpad is created; user can retry from the menu\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"detection\": \"readdir succeeds but a stat on an entry rejects, or an entry is a directory named *.md\",\n          \"recoverable\": true,\n          \"response\": \"listScratches skips entries whose stat fails or that are not files; a fully unreadable dir (non-ENOENT error) surfaces ScratchStoreError and the menu shows the unavailable row\",\n          \"scenario\": \"Corrupt or permission-restricted entries inside ~/.insrc/scratches\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"List degrades to the readable entries instead of failing wholesale\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"detection\": \"panels.create throws or the webview fails to load\",\n          \"recoverable\": true,\n          \"response\": \"Handler never throws (extension.ts:465-468 swallow pattern); error is logged via panelLog and surfaced as a VS Code notification only\",\n          \"scenario\": \"Browse-all or document webview panel cannot be created\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Click does nothing visible except a logged/notification error; chat stays usable\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"detection\": \"postMessage to a disposed webview (chat panel closed while scratchpad document posts send-to-chat)\",\n          \"recoverable\": true,\n          \"response\": \"The swallow pattern at extension.ts:465-468 discards the post; no error propagates\",\n          \"scenario\": \"send-to-chat posted after the chat webview was closed or reloaded\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Nothing is inserted; the selection is simply not delivered that once\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"source\": \"c1\",\n          \"text\": \"The attach flow is untouched: #insrc-attach button, .attachbar, and the 'pick-attachments' host case at chat-panel.ts:3566 keep their exact behavior; the scratchpad button is a sibling, not a modification.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"c1\",\n          \"text\": \"Webview CSP invariant: scratch content is rendered via textContent/escapeHtml only — never innerHTML with user content; new panels reuse the CSP+nonce shell from createWebviewPanelHost (panels/webview-host.ts:162).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"c2\",\n          \"text\": \"Protocol exhaustiveness: every new message type appears in the protocol.ts union AND in both HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES (:378) and WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES (:403) const arrays, which protocol.test.ts asserts exhaustively.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"c3\",\n          \"text\": \"Store pattern: the scratch store stays vscode-free and deps-injected (ScratchFs interface + node impl) exactly like attachment-store.ts, so tests drive it with fakes; root comes from PATHS.insrc (src/shared/paths.ts:4-8), never a hard-coded path.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"c1\",\n          \"text\": \"Send-to-chat never auto-sends a turn: insert-into-input only inserts text into #insrc-prompt (:2783) and focuses it; the user presses send.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source\": \"c4\",\n          \"text\": \"Plain files, no daemon IPC: scratchpads are .md files under ~/.insrc/scratches only; no LMDB/Lance/daemon socket usage is introduced.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"VS Code plugin scratchpads: ~/.insrc/scratches store, chat-input scratchpad button with recent/new/browse-all menu, tabular browse webview, Send-to-chat on text selection\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\"\n      },\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {},\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\"\n    },\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"Fully backward compatible: no existing public API, protocol message, store root, or package.json contribution is changed or removed. The webview→host and host→webview unions only gain new message types (additive); protocol.test.ts's exhaustiveness assertion is updated in the same change. The attach flow, chat-attachments store, and all existing webview panels are untouched. Older extension versions simply have no scratchpad button; no data exists to migrate because ~/.insrc/scratches starts empty.\",\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": false,\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"action\": \"Add the vscode-free scratch-store.ts module (ScratchFs interface + node impl, createScratchStore/listScratches/createScratch/readScratch/deleteScratch) with its unit tests and fake-scratch-fs.ts — new files only, no edits to existing modules\",\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"action\": \"Extend protocol.ts: add the eight new message types to the webview→host and host→webview unions and to both HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES and WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES const arrays; update protocol.test.ts expectations — additive only\",\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"action\": \"Wire the store in extension.ts next to the createAttachmentStore call (~:635): createScratchStore({ root: join(PATHS.insrc, 'scratches'), logger: panelLog }) and register the six new host message handlers plus the insert-into-input push; no changes to existing handlers\",\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"action\": \"Add the chat webview DOM + bootstrap in chat-panel.ts: sibling #insrc-scratch .attachbtn icon button next to #insrc-attach (:2796), #insrc-scratchmenu .popup.chatmenu with recent/New/Browse-all items, the click listener posting scratch-open-menu, and the insert-into-input handler targeting #insrc-prompt (:2783); CSS reuses existing .attachbtn/.popup/.item rules so only minimal new styles are added\",\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"action\": \"Add the two webview viewTypes (insrc.scratchpads tabular browse view, insrc.scratchpad document view with floating Send-to-chat on selection) through the existing injected PanelFactory (extension.ts:447) with the shared CSP+nonce shell from panels/webview-host.ts:162; single-instance create-or-reveal per viewType\",\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"action\": \"Create the scratches root lazily on first write (mkdir recursive inside createScratch); no pre-creation step needed, no existing directory is modified\",\n          \"order\": 6,\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"stateAfter\": \"VS Code plugin ships scratchpads: plain markdown files under ~/.insrc/scratches (created lazily on first use) managed by a vscode-free scratch-store; the chat status bar shows an icon-only scratchpad button next to the attach button whose popup lists the 5 most recent scratchpads plus New scratchpad and Browse all; Browse all opens a single-instance tabular editor-pane webview (Name, Modified, icon-only Open/Delete per row); Open shows the scratchpad in a document webview where selecting text reveals a floating icon-only Send-to-chat button that inserts the selection into the chat input and focuses it (never auto-sends); all eight new protocol messages are additive to the existing unions and type lists; no daemon IPC, no migration of existing data (the dir starts empty).\",\n      \"stateBefore\": \"Per s1 bundles (c1-c4): the chat status bar has only the attach button #insrc-attach (chat-panel.ts:2796) wired to 'pick-attachments' (host switch :3566); the only popup menu is #insrc-histmenu (.popup.chatmenu :2766, wiring :2532-2544); protocol.ts has no scratchpad messages (:346, :378, :403); extension.ts wires only chat-attachments (:635) and chat-sessions (:636) stores under PATHS.insrc (src/shared/paths.ts:4-8) and injects the panels factory at :447 whose core is createWebviewPanelHost (panels/webview-host.ts:162); there is no ~/.insrc/scratches usage anywhere and no scratchpad UI or protocol types exist.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": true\n    },\n    \"openQuestions\": [],\n    \"sequenceDefinition\": {\n      \"id\": \"scratchpad-send-to-chat\",\n      \"messages\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Clicking the scratchpad icon button posts scratch-open-menu to the extension host.\",\n          \"from\": \"chat-webview\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\",\n          \"label\": \"post { type: 'scratch-open-menu' }\",\n          \"to\": \"extension-host\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Host calls listScratches(5) on the scratch store (plain .md files under ~/.insrc/scratches).\",\n          \"from\": \"extension-host\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\",\n          \"label\": \"listScratches(5)\",\n          \"to\": \"scratch-store\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Store returns entries sorted by mtime desc.\",\n          \"from\": \"scratch-store\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"label\": \"ScratchEntry[]\",\n          \"to\": \"extension-host\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Host pushes the recent list to the chat webview, which renders the popup menu (recent + New scratchpad + Browse all).\",\n          \"from\": \"extension-host\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\",\n          \"label\": \"push { type: 'scratch-list', entries }\",\n          \"to\": \"chat-webview\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Selecting a row (or Browse all) posts scratch-open / scratch-browse; host creates-or-reveals the insrc.scratchpad document panel / insrc.scratchpads table panel via the injected panels factory and reads the file.\",\n          \"from\": \"chat-webview\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\",\n          \"label\": \"post { type: 'scratch-open', id } | { type: 'scratch-browse' }\",\n          \"to\": \"extension-host\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Document view renders content via textContent only; on selectionchange with a non-empty selection the floating icon-only Send-to-chat button appears.\",\n          \"from\": \"scratch-doc-view\",\n          \"kind\": \"recurse\",\n          \"label\": \"selectionchange -> show floating button (title=\\\"Send to chat\\\")\",\n          \"to\": \"scratch-doc-view\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Clicking the floating button posts the selected text (capped at 64 KiB) to the host.\",\n          \"from\": \"scratch-doc-view\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\",\n          \"label\": \"post { type: 'send-to-chat', text }\",\n          \"to\": \"extension-host\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Host pushes the text to the chat webview; the chat webview inserts it at the cursor (or appends) of #insrc-prompt and focuses it — the turn is NEVER auto-sent.\",\n          \"from\": \"extension-host\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\",\n          \"label\": \"push { type: 'insert-into-input', text }\",\n          \"to\": \"chat-webview\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Chat webview inserts text into #insrc-prompt and focuses it; user presses send.\",\n          \"from\": \"chat-webview\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"label\": \"insert into #insrc-prompt + focus (no send)\",\n          \"to\": \"extension-host\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"narrative\": \"The Send-to-chat flow crosses three surfaces (scratchpad document view, extension host, chat webview) over the new protocol messages; the diagram pins the ordering and the invariant that text is only inserted into the chat input, never submitted.\",\n      \"participants\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Inline-HTML chat webview: #insrc-scratch button, #insrc-scratchmenu popup, #insrc-prompt input.\",\n          \"id\": \"chat-webview\",\n          \"label\": \"Chat webview\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"VS Code extension host: message switch, scratch store access, panel factory.\",\n          \"id\": \"extension-host\",\n          \"label\": \"Extension host\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Vscode-free store over plain .md files in ~/.insrc/scratches.\",\n          \"id\": \"scratch-store\",\n          \"label\": \"ScratchStore\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"insrc.scratchpad webview panel: document content + floating Send-to-chat button on selection.\",\n          \"id\": \"scratch-doc-view\",\n          \"label\": \"Scratchpad document view\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"truncations\": [\n        {\n          \"atParticipant\": \"extension-host\",\n          \"note\": \"Browse-table open/delete rows post scratch-open/scratch-delete through the same host switch; elided for brevity.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"product\",\n      \"prose\": \"This story adds scratchpads to the VS Code chat: a scratchpad icon button next to the attach button opens a menu with recent scratchpads, a New scratchpad item and a Browse all item. Browse all opens a tabular editor pane (name, date, icon-only open/delete) over the scratchpads stored as plain markdown files in ~/.insrc/scratches. Opening a scratchpad shows its content in an editor pane where selecting text reveals a floating \\\"Send to chat\\\" button that drops the selection into the chat input (never auto-sends). No daemon IPC is added.\"\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"scratch-store.test.ts: listScratches returns entries sorted by mtime desc with id/name/mtime/size\",\n            \"scratch-store.test.ts: createScratch writes <yyyymmdd-hhmmss>-<slug>.md via temp+rename and it appears at list head\",\n            \"extension-chat-wiring.test.ts: extension.ts constructs createScratchStore with root join(PATHS.insrc, 'scratches')\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"chat-panel.test.ts: #insrc-scratch sibling button with class attachbtn + inline SVG + title exists next to #insrc-attach\",\n            \"chat-panel.test.ts: #insrc-scratchmenu .popup.chatmenu renders recent items + New scratchpad + Browse all from a scratch-list push\",\n            \"chat-panel.test.ts: bootstrap click on #insrc-scratch posts {type:'scratch-open-menu'}\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"scratch-panel.test.ts: browse viewType insrc.scratchpads renders a table with Name and Modified columns\",\n            \"scratch-panel.test.ts: each row has icon-only Open/Delete buttons (title hover text, data-id) posting scratch-open/scratch-delete\",\n            \"scratch-panel.test.ts: empty list renders a hint row; create-or-reveal reuses a single panel instance\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac4\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"scratch-panel.test.ts: document viewType insrc.scratchpad renders content via textContent only\",\n            \"scratch-panel.test.ts: selectionchange with non-empty selection shows the floating icon-only Send-to-chat button (title) which posts send-to-chat {text}\",\n            \"chat-panel.test.ts: host insert-into-input handler inserts text at cursor/appends to #insrc-prompt and focuses it without sending\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac5\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"chat-panel.test.ts + scratch-panel.test.ts: every button in the new UI is icon-only with a title attribute (assert no visible text content on buttons)\",\n            \"protocol.test.ts: all eight new message types appear in the union and both const arrays (exhaustiveness assertion passes)\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test + node:assert/strict via npx tsx --test (repo convention; vscode-plugin suites run with the default node, daemon suites need node 22 on PATH)\",\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"fake-scratch-fs.ts (in-memory ScratchFs, mirrors fake-attachment-fs.ts)\",\n            \"fixed clock injected via deps.now for deterministic yyyymmdd-hhmmss names\"\n          ],\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Prove the vscode-free store contract: list/create/read/delete over ~/.insrc/scratches, sorting, slug naming, collision suffixes, temp+rename writes, id validation, ENOENT→[] / idempotent delete, error mapping (ScratchRefused/ScratchNotFound/ScratchStoreError)\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/scratch-store.ts (new)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/scratch-store.test.ts (new)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fake-scratch-fs.ts (new)\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"fake-dom.ts (existing)\",\n            \"a fake panels factory recording create() calls by viewType/title\"\n          ],\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Prove the wiring: protocol type exhaustiveness, chat webview button+menu markup and bootstrap posts, host switch cases for all six webview→host messages and both host→webview pushes, panel create-or-reveal for both viewTypes, insert-into-input behavior on #insrc-prompt, and the floating Send-to-chat button on selection in the document view\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts (extended)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts (button, menu, bootstrap, host cases)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts (exhaustiveness)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts (button/menu/insert-into-input)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/scratch-panel.test.ts (new: browse table + document view + floating button)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/extension-chat-wiring.test.ts (store root wiring next to extension.ts:635)\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts (createScratchStore wiring + handler registration)\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"none — no live daemon or network is touched; scratchpads are plain files\"\n          ],\n          \"level\": \"smoke\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Smoke the real extension host path only if a display/VS Code test harness is available; otherwise covered by the integration fake-dom suite. No live LLM or daemon calls — the feature adds zero daemon IPC\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"manual/optional smoke: click scratchpad button in the chat status bar, create a scratchpad, browse all, select text, Send to chat\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"uxDefinition\": {\n      \"body\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Chat status-bar input row: the existing attach icon button, and directly next to it the new scratchpad icon button (same .attachbtn family, inline SVG icon, title=\\\"scratchpads\\\" hover text, no visible label).\",\n          \"text\": \"Chat input row: [attach icon button] [scratchpad icon button] [prompt input] [send]\",\n          \"type\": \"TextBlock\",\n          \"wrap\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Popup that opens upward from the scratchpad button (existing .popup.chatmenu pattern): up to 5 most-recent scratchpad rows (click = open), then a \\\"New scratchpad\\\" row, then a \\\"Browse all\\\" row.\",\n          \"text\": \"Scratchpads popup: recent-1 … recent-5 | New scratchpad | Browse all\",\n          \"type\": \"TextBlock\",\n          \"wrap\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Editor-area webview panel (viewType insrc.scratchpads) listing every scratchpad as a table row: Name column, Modified (date) column, and two icon-only buttons per row — Open and Delete — each carrying a title hover text and data-id; no text labels on the buttons.\",\n          \"text\": \"Browse-all editor pane table: [Name] [Modified] [open icon btn] [delete icon btn]\",\n          \"type\": \"TextBlock\",\n          \"wrap\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Editor-area webview panel (viewType insrc.scratchpad) showing one scratchpad's content (rendered via textContent only); when the user selects text, a floating icon-only button with title=\\\"Send to chat\\\" appears near the selection; clicking it inserts the selection into the chat input (never auto-sends).\",\n          \"text\": \"Scratchpad document pane with floating icon-only \\\"Send to chat\\\" button on text selection\",\n          \"type\": \"TextBlock\",\n          \"wrap\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"narrative\": \"The story introduces three user-facing surfaces — the status-bar button+popup, the tabular browse pane, and the document pane with its floating selection button — and pins that every button is icon-only with hover text (title), matching the user's requirement.\",\n      \"type\": \"AdaptiveCard\",\n      \"version\": \"1.4\"\n    },\n    \"companions\": [\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"ux-mock\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ux-mock.html\",\n        \"title\": \"UX mock\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"diagram-mermaid\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/sequence-diagram.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Sequence diagram\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"diagram-mermaid\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/component-dependency.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Component dependencies\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"s1 analyze bundle c1 (chat webview status bar): the status bar already hosts the icon-only attach button at :2796 with .attachbtn class and inline SVG; a scratchpad button slots in as a sibling with the same class family; the existing popup pattern is #insrc-histmenu .popup.chatmenu at :2766 wired at :2532-2544; host switch case 'pick-attachments' at :3566; bootstrap wiring at :2465-2486; #insrc-prompt at :2783.\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2796\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"s1 analyze bundle c2 (protocol): webview→host union at :346, HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES at :378, WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES at :403, const arrays asserted for exhaustiveness in protocol.test.ts — new scratchpad messages are added to both the unions and the const lists.\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:346\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"s1 analyze bundle c3 (extension wiring): extension.ts:635 constructs createAttachmentStore({ root: join(PATHS.insrc, 'chat-attachments'), logger }); panels factory injected at extension.ts:447 via vscode.window.createWebviewPanel(viewType, title, column, { enableScripts: true }); VS-Code-free core createWebviewPanelHost at panels/webview-host.ts:162 with types in panels/types.ts.\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:635\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"s1 analyze bundle c4 (store pattern + tests): attachment-store.ts is a vscode-free deps-injected module with an AttachmentFs interface and node impl; tests inject fake-attachment-fs.ts; chat-panel.test.ts + fake-dom.ts drive the inline-HTML bootstrap; protocol.test.ts asserts type-list exhaustiveness; suites run via npx tsx --test with node:test + node:assert/strict.\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"PATHS.insrc is join(homedir(), '.insrc') — the scratches root derives from it, never a hard-coded path.\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/shared/paths.ts:4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"CSP+nonce shell and single-instance create-or-reveal lifecycle shared by all webview panels; the two new scratch viewTypes reuse it.\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:162\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"Protocol type lists asserted exhaustively — every new message type must appear in the union and both const arrays.\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-4642d49ab0593787-s1 — VS Code plugin scratchpads: ~/.insrc/scratches store, chat-input scratchpad button with recent/new/browse-all menu, tabular browse webview, Send-to-chat on text selection\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794551362794-fdm5ky`\n**HLD effective hash:** `4642d49ab059...`\n\nThis story adds scratchpads to the VS Code chat: a scratchpad icon button next to the attach button opens a menu with recent scratchpads, a New scratchpad item and a Browse all item. Browse all opens a tabular editor pane (name, date, icon-only open/delete) over the scratchpads stored as plain markdown files in ~/.insrc/scratches. Opening a scratchpad shows its content in an editor pane where selecting text reveals a floating \"Send to chat\" button that drops the selection into the chat input (never auto-sends). No daemon IPC is added.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Diagrams](#4-diagrams)\n5. [Error paths](#5-error-paths)\n6. [Test strategy](#6-test-strategy)\n7. [Migration](#7-migration)\n8. [Alternatives considered](#8-alternatives-considered)\n9. [UX](#9-ux)\n10. [References](#10-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** public\n\n### 2.1 `createScratchStore`\n\n```typescript\nfunction createScratchStore(deps: ScratchStoreDeps): ScratchStore\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `deps: { root: string; fs: ScratchFs; now?: () => Date; logger?: Logger }` — Deps-injected root + fs + clock, mirroring createAttachmentStore at vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:635 (root = join(PATHS.insrc, 'scratches'), PATHS.insrc = join(homedir(), '.insrc') per src/shared/paths.ts:4-8)\n\n**Returns:** `ScratchStore` — Store handle exposing list/create/read/delete; vscode-free so fake-dom/fake-fs tests can drive it\n\n**Errors:**\n- `ScratchStoreError` when root path is not a directory or mkdir fails (EACCES/ENOSPC)\n- `ScratchRefused` when id fails the ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ validation\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- deps.root is an absolute path under ~/.insrc\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Store is ready; the scratches root exists or is created lazily on first write\n- No daemon IPC is involved — pure filesystem\n\n### 2.2 `listScratches`\n\n```typescript\nfunction listScratches(limit?: number): Promise<ScratchEntry[]>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `limit?: number | undefined` _(optional)_ — Cap the returned list (menu shows top 5 recent by mtime; browse-all passes no limit)\n\n**Returns:** `ScratchEntry[]` — Metadata for every ~/.insrc/scratches/*.md file\n\n**Errors:**\n- `returns [] (empty list, not an error)` when readdir ENOENT (no scratches dir yet)\n- `ScratchStoreError` when readdir EACCES/other\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Store created via createScratchStore\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Entries are sorted by mtime descending (most recent first)\n- Each entry carries id, name, mtime and size; ids are the file basenames\n\n### 2.3 `createScratch`\n\n```typescript\nfunction createScratch(title: string, body?: string): Promise<ScratchEntry>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `title: string` — Human title for the new scratchpad; slugified into the file name\n- `body?: string | undefined` _(optional)_ — Initial content; omitted = a short starter line inviting notes\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<ScratchEntry>` — The created entry's metadata\n\n**Errors:**\n- `ScratchStoreError` when slug collision after the -2/-3 suffix ladder\n- `ScratchStoreError` when write EACCES/ENOSPC\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- title is a non-empty string\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A new file <yyyymmdd-hhmmss>-<slug>.md exists under the root (collision suffixes -2, -3, ...)\n- Write is temp-file + rename so no partial file is ever visible\n- The new entry appears at the head of listScratches\n\n### 2.4 `readScratch`\n\n```typescript\nfunction readScratch(id: string): Promise<{ entry: ScratchEntry; content: string }>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — File basename of the scratchpad to open in the document view\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<{ entry: ScratchEntry; content: string }>` — Full text content plus entry metadata\n\n**Errors:**\n- `ScratchRefused` when id fails ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ validation\n- `ScratchNotFound` when read ENOENT (already deleted)\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Store created; id matches the validation regex before any fs call\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The full markdown content is returned for rendering\n- Content is rendered via textContent/escapeHtml only — CSP invariant kept\n\n### 2.5 `deleteScratch`\n\n```typescript\nfunction deleteScratch(id: string): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — File basename to delete from the browse table row or the document view\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<void>` — Void\n\n**Errors:**\n- `ScratchRefused` when id fails ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ validation\n- `treated as success (delete is idempotent)` when rm ENOENT\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Store created; id matches the validation regex before any fs call\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The file is gone (or was already gone) and drops out of listScratches\n- Deleting the currently open document closes that panel\n\n### 2.6 `chat host message handlers (switch on payload.type, chat-panel.ts:3566 pattern)`\n\n```typescript\nhandleChatMessage(msg: WebviewToHostMessage): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `msg: WebviewToHostMessage | HostToWebviewMessage` — Webview→host messages 'scratch-open-menu' | 'scratch-new' | 'scratch-open' {id} | 'scratch-delete' {id} | 'scratch-browse' | 'send-to-chat' {text}; host→webview 'scratch-list' {entries} | 'insert-into-input' {text} — all added to the protocol.ts unions (:346) and both const lists HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES (:378) / WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES (:403), exhaustiveness asserted in protocol.test.ts\n\n**Returns:** `void` — Side effects on panels + webviews; no return value\n\n**Errors:**\n- `ignored (never throws — postMessage failures are swallowed per extension.ts:465-468 pattern)` when unknown payload.type in the host switch\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Chat panel is alive; scratch store is wired in extension.ts next to :635\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- 'scratch-open-menu' replies with 'scratch-list' of the top 5\n- 'scratch-new' creates a scratchpad and replies with 'scratch-list' + opens the document view\n- 'scratch-open' opens/creates-or-reveals the insrc.scratchpad document panel\n- 'scratch-delete' deletes then refreshes any open browse table\n- 'scratch-browse' opens/creates-or-reveals the insrc.scratchpads table panel\n- 'send-to-chat' pushes 'insert-into-input' {text} to the chat webview; text capped at 64 KiB with '…' truncation\n\n### 2.7 `webview panels via the injected PanelFactory (extension.ts:447)`\n\n```typescript\npanels.create(viewType: ScratchViewType, title: string): WebviewPanel\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `viewType: 'insrc.scratchpads' | 'insrc.scratchpad'` — insrc.scratchpads = browse-all tabular view (columns Name, Modified; icon-only Open/Delete buttons with title tooltips + data-id); insrc.scratchpad = single-document view with a selectionchange listener\n- `title: string` — Panel title (scratchpad name for the document view)\n\n**Returns:** `WebviewPanel` — A webview panel handle\n\n**Errors:**\n- `never throws; logged via panelLog` when panel creation failure\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- panels factory injected at extension.ts:447 (vscode.window.createWebviewPanel(viewType, title, ViewColumn.Active, { enableScripts: true }))\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Panels use the shared CSP+nonce shell from createWebviewPanelHost (panels/webview-host.ts:162) and the single-instance create-or-reveal lifecycle\n- Browse table rows post 'scratch-open' {id} / 'scratch-delete' {id}\n- Document view posts 'send-to-chat' {text} from its floating button on non-empty selection\n\n### 2.8 `floating Send-to-chat button (document view bootstrap)`\n\n```typescript\nonSelectionChange(sel: Selection): void\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `sel: Selection` — window.getSelection() on selectionchange inside the insrc.scratchpad document view; button is icon-only with title=\"Send to chat\"\n\n**Returns:** `void` — UI side effect only\n\n**Errors:**\n- `floating button stays hidden` when selection empty or collapsed\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Document view is open and has focus\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A floating button appears near the selection and posts { type: 'send-to-chat', text } to the host\n- Host pushes 'insert-into-input' to the chat webview, which inserts the text at the cursor (or appends) of #insrc-prompt (chat-panel.ts:2783) and focuses it — NEVER auto-sends a turn\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `ScratchEntry / scratchpad file under ~/.insrc/scratches` — new\n\nScratchEntry { id, name, mtime, size } — metadata for one ~/.insrc/scratches/<yyyymmdd-hhmmss>-<slug>.md file. id = file basename, validated ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ before any fs call. Stored as plain markdown files; no daemon store, no LMDB/Lance row. Entries are enumerated by readdir + stat (ENOENT → []), sorted by mtime desc, optionally limited (menu top 5).\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:635`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:636`\n- `src/shared/paths.ts:4`\n- `src/shared/paths.ts:8`\n\n### 3.2 `Webview↔host protocol messages (protocol.ts)` — new\n\nEight new message types added to the webview↔host unions and BOTH const arrays (exhaustiveness asserted in protocol.test.ts): webview→host 'scratch-open-menu', 'scratch-new', 'scratch-open' {id}, 'scratch-delete' {id}, 'scratch-browse', 'send-to-chat' {text}; host→webview 'scratch-list' {entries}, 'insert-into-input' {text}. Payload field names are part of the contract.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:346`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:378`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:403`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts`\n\n### 3.3 `Chat status-bar UI: scratchpad button + popup menu + input insertion` — new\n\nChat webview DOM additions: a sibling icon-only button #insrc-scratch (class attachbtn, inline SVG, title=\"scratchpads\") directly next to #insrc-attach (:2796); a dropdown #insrc-scratchmenu reusing the .popup.chatmenu / .item pattern of #insrc-histmenu (:2766, opens upward :2289, rows :2296) whose items are recent entries + \"New scratchpad\" + \"Browse all\"; one bootstrap listener (:2465-2486 pattern) posting 'scratch-open-menu'; the host 'insert-into-input' handler inserts text into #insrc-prompt (:2783) and focuses it. Attach flow (.attachbar :2787, 'pick-attachments' :3566) untouched.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2796`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2766`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2289`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2296`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2465`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2486`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3566`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2783`\n\n### 3.4 `Scratchpad webview panel viewTypes` — new\n\nTwo new webview viewTypes through the existing injected PanelFactory: 'insrc.scratchpads' (browse-all tabular editor-pane view: columns Name and Modified, per-row icon-only Open/Delete buttons with title hover text and data-id) and 'insrc.scratchpad' (single-document view rendering scratch content via textContent only, with the selectionchange → floating icon-only \"Send to chat\" button). Both keep the shared CSP+nonce shell and create-or-reveal single-instance lifecycle.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:162`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/panels/types.ts`\n\n## 4. Diagrams\n\n- [Sequence diagram](docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/sequence-diagram.html)\n- [Component dependencies](docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/component-dependency.html)\n\n## 5. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **~/.insrc/scratches cannot be created or written (read-only home, disk full, permissions)** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: fs.mkdir/readdir/writeFile rejects with code EACCES, ENOSPC, EROFS, or the root is not a directory\n  - Response: createScratchStore/list/create surface ScratchStoreError; the host handler catches, logs via panelLog and shows a menu row 'scratchpads unavailable: <reason>'; menu still offers Browse all, which shows an error row\n  - User impact: Scratchpads cannot be listed/created; the attach flow and chat itself keep working (failure is contained to the scratch features)\n- **Malicious or malformed id in a webview message (path traversal ../, separators, metacharacters)** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: id fails the ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ check before any fs call\n  - Response: readScratch/deleteScratch throw ScratchRefused; host logs and ignores the message — no filesystem access happens\n  - User impact: No impact; the attempt is refused and logged\n- **Opening or deleting a scratchpad whose file was deleted out-of-band while the menu/table was showing** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: readFile on the id rejects with ENOENT\n  - Response: readScratch maps ENOENT to ScratchNotFound; host closes the document panel (if open) and refreshes the browse table so the stale row disappears\n  - User impact: Stale menu/table row resolves on next interaction; no crash\n- **Crash or EACCES/ENOSPC between temp write and rename during createScratch** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: writeFile of the temp file or the rename fails mid-create\n  - Response: ScratchStoreError surfaces to the host; the temp file is best-effort removed; no partial .md file is left visible (temp name does not match the *.md listing filter)\n  - User impact: No scratchpad is created; user can retry from the menu\n- **Corrupt or permission-restricted entries inside ~/.insrc/scratches** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: readdir succeeds but a stat on an entry rejects, or an entry is a directory named *.md\n  - Response: listScratches skips entries whose stat fails or that are not files; a fully unreadable dir (non-ENOENT error) surfaces ScratchStoreError and the menu shows the unavailable row\n  - User impact: List degrades to the readable entries instead of failing wholesale\n- **Browse-all or document webview panel cannot be created** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: panels.create throws or the webview fails to load\n  - Response: Handler never throws (extension.ts:465-468 swallow pattern); error is logged via panelLog and surfaced as a VS Code notification only\n  - User impact: Click does nothing visible except a logged/notification error; chat stays usable\n- **send-to-chat posted after the chat webview was closed or reloaded** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: postMessage to a disposed webview (chat panel closed while scratchpad document posts send-to-chat)\n  - Response: The swallow pattern at extension.ts:465-468 discards the post; no error propagates\n  - User impact: Nothing is inserted; the selection is simply not delivered that once\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| No ~/.insrc/scratches directory exists yet (fresh install) — readdir ENOENT | listScratches returns [] — the menu shows only \"New scratchpad\" + \"Browse all\", and Browse all shows an empty table with a hint row |\n| Two scratchpads created within the same second from the same title (yyyymmdd-hhmmss-slug collision) | File name gets a -2 (then -3, ...) suffix and the entry is created without error |\n| Title containing unicode, spaces, slashes or other non-slug characters | createScratch slugifies the title (lowercase, spaces to dashes, non [a-z0-9-] dropped) so the generated id always matches ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$; an all-symbol title falls back to 'scratch' |\n| A file in ~/.insrc/scratches disappears between readdir and stat | The entry is skipped from the list (not a crash); an entry whose stat fails is dropped rather than failing the whole list |\n| Directory contains unrelated files (e.g. .DS_Store, a leftover .tmp) | Non-.md files in the scratches dir are ignored by listScratches; the temp file from an interrupted write is ignored (its name does not end in .md) |\n| User selects more than 64 KiB of text in the scratchpad document view | send-to-chat is accepted up to 64 KiB; larger selections are truncated at 64 KiB with a trailing ellipsis and still inserted |\n| A webview-to-host scratch-open/scratch-delete payload carries an id with path separators or shell metacharacters (../, ;, spaces) | readScratch/deleteScratch refuse before touching the filesystem (ScratchRefused); the host handler logs and ignores the message |\n| User double-clicks Delete on the same browse-table row | Deleting an already-deleted id resolves successfully; the browse table just re-renders without the row |\n| The scratchpad file backing an open insrc.scratchpad document view is deleted (from the browse table or the filesystem) | The document panel closes (or shows an empty state) and the entry disappears from the browse table on next refresh |\n| Chat input #insrc-prompt already contains unsent text when insert-into-input arrives | insert-into-input appends at the end of the existing prompt text (with a separating newline when the input is non-empty) and focuses #insrc-prompt; the turn is NOT sent |\n| User clicks into the document without selecting any text (collapsed selection) and selectionchange fires | The floating button stays hidden; nothing is posted |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- The attach flow is untouched: #insrc-attach button, .attachbar, and the 'pick-attachments' host case at chat-panel.ts:3566 keep their exact behavior; the scratchpad button is a sibling, not a modification. [[c1]]\n- Webview CSP invariant: scratch content is rendered via textContent/escapeHtml only — never innerHTML with user content; new panels reuse the CSP+nonce shell from createWebviewPanelHost (panels/webview-host.ts:162). [[c1]]\n- Protocol exhaustiveness: every new message type appears in the protocol.ts union AND in both HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES (:378) and WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES (:403) const arrays, which protocol.test.ts asserts exhaustively. [[c2]]\n- Store pattern: the scratch store stays vscode-free and deps-injected (ScratchFs interface + node impl) exactly like attachment-store.ts, so tests drive it with fakes; root comes from PATHS.insrc (src/shared/paths.ts:4-8), never a hard-coded path. [[c3]]\n- Send-to-chat never auto-sends a turn: insert-into-input only inserts text into #insrc-prompt (:2783) and focuses it; the user presses send. [[c1]]\n- Plain files, no daemon IPC: scratchpads are .md files under ~/.insrc/scratches only; no LMDB/Lance/daemon socket usage is introduced. [[c4]]\n\n## 6. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test + node:assert/strict via npx tsx --test (repo convention; vscode-plugin suites run with the default node, daemon suites need node 22 on PATH)`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — Prove the vscode-free store contract: list/create/read/delete over ~/.insrc/scratches, sorting, slug naming, collision suffixes, temp+rename writes, id validation, ENOENT→[] / idempotent delete, error mapping (ScratchRefused/ScratchNotFound/ScratchStoreError)\n  - Subjects: `vscode-plugin/src/chat/scratch-store.ts (new)`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/scratch-store.test.ts (new)`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fake-scratch-fs.ts (new)`\n  - Fixtures: `fake-scratch-fs.ts (in-memory ScratchFs, mirrors fake-attachment-fs.ts)`, `fixed clock injected via deps.now for deterministic yyyymmdd-hhmmss names`\n- **integration** — Prove the wiring: protocol type exhaustiveness, chat webview button+menu markup and bootstrap posts, host switch cases for all six webview→host messages and both host→webview pushes, panel create-or-reveal for both viewTypes, insert-into-input behavior on #insrc-prompt, and the floating Send-to-chat button on selection in the document view\n  - Subjects: `vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts (extended)`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts (button, menu, bootstrap, host cases)`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts (exhaustiveness)`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts (button/menu/insert-into-input)`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/scratch-panel.test.ts (new: browse table + document view + floating button)`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/extension-chat-wiring.test.ts (store root wiring next to extension.ts:635)`, `vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts (createScratchStore wiring + handler registration)`\n  - Fixtures: `fake-dom.ts (existing)`, `a fake panels factory recording create() calls by viewType/title`\n- **smoke** — Smoke the real extension host path only if a display/VS Code test harness is available; otherwise covered by the integration fake-dom suite. No live LLM or daemon calls — the feature adds zero daemon IPC\n  - Subjects: `manual/optional smoke: click scratchpad button in the chat status bar, create a scratchpad, browse all, select text, Send to chat`\n  - Fixtures: `none — no live daemon or network is touched; scratchpads are plain files`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `scratch-store.test.ts: listScratches returns entries sorted by mtime desc with id/name/mtime/size`, `scratch-store.test.ts: createScratch writes <yyyymmdd-hhmmss>-<slug>.md via temp+rename and it appears at list head`, `extension-chat-wiring.test.ts: extension.ts constructs createScratchStore with root join(PATHS.insrc, 'scratches')` |\n| `ac2` | `chat-panel.test.ts: #insrc-scratch sibling button with class attachbtn + inline SVG + title exists next to #insrc-attach`, `chat-panel.test.ts: #insrc-scratchmenu .popup.chatmenu renders recent items + New scratchpad + Browse all from a scratch-list push`, `chat-panel.test.ts: bootstrap click on #insrc-scratch posts {type:'scratch-open-menu'}` |\n| `ac3` | `scratch-panel.test.ts: browse viewType insrc.scratchpads renders a table with Name and Modified columns`, `scratch-panel.test.ts: each row has icon-only Open/Delete buttons (title hover text, data-id) posting scratch-open/scratch-delete`, `scratch-panel.test.ts: empty list renders a hint row; create-or-reveal reuses a single panel instance` |\n| `ac4` | `scratch-panel.test.ts: document viewType insrc.scratchpad renders content via textContent only`, `scratch-panel.test.ts: selectionchange with non-empty selection shows the floating icon-only Send-to-chat button (title) which posts send-to-chat {text}`, `chat-panel.test.ts: host insert-into-input handler inserts text at cursor/appends to #insrc-prompt and focuses it without sending` |\n| `ac5` | `chat-panel.test.ts + scratch-panel.test.ts: every button in the new UI is icon-only with a title attribute (assert no visible text content on buttons)`, `protocol.test.ts: all eight new message types appear in the union and both const arrays (exhaustiveness assertion passes)` |\n\n## 7. Migration\n\n**State before:** Per s1 bundles (c1-c4): the chat status bar has only the attach button #insrc-attach (chat-panel.ts:2796) wired to 'pick-attachments' (host switch :3566); the only popup menu is #insrc-histmenu (.popup.chatmenu :2766, wiring :2532-2544); protocol.ts has no scratchpad messages (:346, :378, :403); extension.ts wires only chat-attachments (:635) and chat-sessions (:636) stores under PATHS.insrc (src/shared/paths.ts:4-8) and injects the panels factory at :447 whose core is createWebviewPanelHost (panels/webview-host.ts:162); there is no ~/.insrc/scratches usage anywhere and no scratchpad UI or protocol types exist.\n\n**State after:** VS Code plugin ships scratchpads: plain markdown files under ~/.insrc/scratches (created lazily on first use) managed by a vscode-free scratch-store; the chat status bar shows an icon-only scratchpad button next to the attach button whose popup lists the 5 most recent scratchpads plus New scratchpad and Browse all; Browse all opens a single-instance tabular editor-pane webview (Name, Modified, icon-only Open/Delete per row); Open shows the scratchpad in a document webview where selecting text reveals a floating icon-only Send-to-chat button that inserts the selection into the chat input and focuses it (never auto-sends); all eight new protocol messages are additive to the existing unions and type lists; no daemon IPC, no migration of existing data (the dir starts empty).\n\n**Zero downtime:** yes — **Data rewrite:** no\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Add the vscode-free scratch-store.ts module (ScratchFs interface + node impl, createScratchStore/listScratches/createScratch/readScratch/deleteScratch) with its unit tests and fake-scratch-fs.ts — new files only, no edits to existing modules — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Extend protocol.ts: add the eight new message types to the webview→host and host→webview unions and to both HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES and WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES const arrays; update protocol.test.ts expectations — additive only — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Wire the store in extension.ts next to the createAttachmentStore call (~:635): createScratchStore({ root: join(PATHS.insrc, 'scratches'), logger: panelLog }) and register the six new host message handlers plus the insert-into-input push; no changes to existing handlers — ↩ rollbackable\n4. Add the chat webview DOM + bootstrap in chat-panel.ts: sibling #insrc-scratch .attachbtn icon button next to #insrc-attach (:2796), #insrc-scratchmenu .popup.chatmenu with recent/New/Browse-all items, the click listener posting scratch-open-menu, and the insert-into-input handler targeting #insrc-prompt (:2783); CSS reuses existing .attachbtn/.popup/.item rules so only minimal new styles are added — ↩ rollbackable\n5. Add the two webview viewTypes (insrc.scratchpads tabular browse view, insrc.scratchpad document view with floating Send-to-chat on selection) through the existing injected PanelFactory (extension.ts:447) with the shared CSP+nonce shell from panels/webview-host.ts:162; single-instance create-or-reveal per viewType — ↩ rollbackable\n6. Create the scratches root lazily on first write (mkdir recursive inside createScratch); no pre-creation step needed, no existing directory is modified — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** Fully backward compatible: no existing public API, protocol message, store root, or package.json contribution is changed or removed. The webview→host and host→webview unions only gain new message types (additive); protocol.test.ts's exhaustiveness assertion is updated in the same change. The attach flow, chat-attachments store, and all existing webview panels are untouched. Older extension versions simply have no scratchpad button; no data exists to migrate because ~/.insrc/scratches starts empty.\n\n## 8. Alternatives considered\n\n### 8.1 a1: Chat-webview menu + dedicated scratchpad webview panels (all-in-plugin, plain files) — **CHOSEN**\n\nSmallest fully-meeting shape: reuse the chat popup for the menu, new webview viewTypes for browse-all and the scratchpad document with floating Send-to-chat; storage via a new vscode-free scratch-store over ~/.insrc/scratches.\n\nOne new vscode-free module `vscode-plugin/src/chat/scratch-store.ts` (ScratchFs + node impl; list/create/read/delete over `~/.insrc/scratches/*.md` named `<yyyymmdd-hhmmss>-<slug>.md`), wired in extension.ts next to the attachment store as `join(PATHS.insrc, 'scratches')`. Chat webview: sibling `.attachbtn`-class icon button `#insrc-scratch` next to `#insrc-attach` opening the existing `.popup`/`.item` menu with recent items (top 5 by mtime), New, and Browse-all rows; new message types in protocol.ts. Browse-all = new webview panel viewType `insrc.scratchpads` via the injected PanelFactory with a name/date/icon-only open-delete table. Opening a scratchpad = document viewType `insrc.scratchpad` with a floating Send-to-chat button on selection posting `send-to-chat`; host pushes `insert-into-input`; the chat webview inserts the text and focuses the input.\n\n### 8.2 a2: Native QuickPick + text-document editor with command-based send-to-chat\n\nHost-side QuickPick menu and a real text editor for scratchpads; selection send-to-chat via command rather than a floating webview button.\n\nVS Code native `window.showQuickPick` for the menu (host-side), `window.createWebviewPanel` for the browse-all table, `vscode.window.showTextDocument` for opening a scratchpad (a real editor), Send-to-chat as a registered command on a status-bar affordance.\n\n**Rejected because:** Rank 3: a native QuickPick moves the menu out of the requested in-panel location next to attach, and a real text document cannot show the required floating Send-to-chat button on selection — the defining interaction is violated.\n\n### 8.3 a3: Sidebar tree view for browse-all + webview reader\n\nRegister a scratchpads TreeDataProvider in a sidebar; chat button opens recent/new; tree provides browse-all and open/delete.\n\nScratchpads as a sidebar tree view (`TreeDataProvider` over ~/.insrc/scratches); chat button only for new/recent; browse-all = the tree itself; open renders in a webview reader pane.\n\n**Rejected because:** Rank 4: a sidebar TreeDataProvider is not the requested editor-pane tabular view with per-row icon-only open/delete buttons, and adds an unrequested package.json views contribution (L cost).\n\n### 8.4 a4: Single-webview overlay for browse + view\n\nMenu in chat webview; browse-all and scratchpad viewing as overlays within the same chat webview.\n\nChat-webview popup for the menu, but browse-all and single-scratchpad viewing rendered as overlay panes inside the SAME chat webview (no separate panel), with the Send-to-chat floating button inside that overlay.\n\n**Rejected because:** Rank 2: an overlay inside the chat webview is not an editor-pane panel, and selection handling there collides with the existing in-chat selection-decision/edit-mode feature.\n\n## 9. UX\n\n- [UX mock](docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ux-mock.html)\n\n## 10. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2796` — \"s1 analyze bundle c1 (chat webview status bar): the status bar already hosts the icon-only attach button at :2796 with .attachbtn class and inline SVG; a scratchpad button slots in as a sibling with t\"\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:346` — \"s1 analyze bundle c2 (protocol): webview→host union at :346, HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES at :378, WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES at :403, const arrays asserted for exhaustiveness in protocol.test.ts — new scratchpad\"\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:635` — \"s1 analyze bundle c3 (extension wiring): extension.ts:635 constructs createAttachmentStore({ root: join(PATHS.insrc, 'chat-attachments'), logger }); panels factory injected at extension.ts:447 via vsc\"\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:1` — \"s1 analyze bundle c4 (store pattern + tests): attachment-store.ts is a vscode-free deps-injected module with an AttachmentFs interface and node impl; tests inject fake-attachment-fs.ts; chat-panel.tes\"\n- **[[c5]]** `code` `src/shared/paths.ts:4` — \"PATHS.insrc is join(homedir(), '.insrc') — the scratches root derives from it, never a hard-coded path.\"\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:162` — \"CSP+nonce shell and single-instance create-or-reveal lifecycle shared by all webview panels; the two new scratch viewTypes reuse it.\"\n- **[[c7]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts` — \"Protocol type lists asserted exhaustively — every new message type must appear in the union and both const arrays.\"\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-13T06:39:00.272Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition","title":"componentDependencyDefinition","kind":"visual"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition","title":"sequenceDefinition","kind":"visual"},{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/uxDefinition","selector":"/body/uxDefinition","title":"uxDefinition","kind":"visual"},{"id":"/body/companions","selector":"/body/companions","title":"companions","kind":"visual"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","title":"a3","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","title":"a4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","title":"scratch-store","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","title":"protocol","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","title":"chat-panel","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","title":"extension","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","title":"panels","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","title":"paths","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","title":"chat-webview","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","title":"extension-host","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","title":"scratch-store","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","title":"scratch-doc-view","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/5","selector":"/citations/5","title":"Citation 6","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/6","selector":"/citations/6","title":"Citation 7","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:26","selector":"document:line:26","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"},{"id":"document:line:261","selector":"document:line:261","title":"4. Diagrams","kind":"section"},{"id":"document:line:401","selector":"document:line:401","title":"9. UX","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The selected a1 approach covers the captured standalone scope: recent/new/browse navigation, a tabular editor pane, selection-to-chat insertion without auto-send, and plain filesystem storage without daemon IPC. No parent HLD or SPEC is declared. Extension ownership and reuse of existing file-store patterns are consistent with the repository boundaries. No blocking defect was demonstrated in the assigned scope sections.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","document:line:26","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:1-95","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447-478","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:631-640","src/shared/paths.ts:1-8","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:340-348"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define ac1–ac5 explicitly alongside the captured scope; the acceptance mapping currently identifies them only through their proving tests.","State whether editing existing scratchpad content inside the plugin is outside this increment. The selected approach specifies a document reader and create/read/delete storage operations."]},{"chunkId":"store","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The persistence design covers lazy initialization, filesystem errors, enumeration and test seams, but its identifier validation permits directory targets and its creation protocol lacks collision-safe publication across writers.","findings":[{"id":"store-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/contractDetails/api — readScratch/deleteScratch; /body/dataModelChanges/0","message":"The prescribed ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ validator accepts both '.' and '..'. Joining these ids to the store root targets the scratches directory itself or its ~/.insrc parent, violating the plain-scratchpad-file boundary. This is especially dangerous because the referenced attachment-store adapter implements rm with recursive:true. Require a scratchpad filename, explicitly reject dot segments, enforce containment and file-only deletion, and test that invalid ids cause no filesystem calls. Specify handling of symlinks so reads cannot follow a scratch entry outside the root.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:115","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:137","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:223","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:61","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:95","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/attachment-store.test.ts — remove rejects '.' and '..'","Read-only Node evaluation confirmed the specified regex accepts '..' and path.join('/home/u/.insrc/scratches', '..') resolves to '/home/u/.insrc'."]},{"id":"store-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api — createScratch; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases","message":"The design combines second-resolution names, a suffix collision ladder and temp-file-plus-rename publication without defining exclusive destination reservation or coordination. Two creates for the same title, including creates from separate VS Code windows sharing PATHS.insrc, can choose the same available basename; ordinary rename can replace the first completed scratchpad with the second. Define unique temporary names and a publication mechanism that cannot overwrite an existing destination, with collision retries covering independent store instances. Include an interleaved concurrent-create test proving both contents survive.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:98","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:99","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:304","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:330","src/shared/paths.ts:4","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:125"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","/citations/3","/citations/4","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/attachment-store.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fake-attachment-fs.ts","src/shared/paths.ts","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:628"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define ScratchEntry field types and derivation explicitly: name after restart, mtime units, byte-size semantics and deterministic ordering when modification times tie.","Align ScratchStoreDeps with the activation example: the contract requires fs, while migration wiring omits it. The referenced attachment store makes fs optional and defaults to its Node adapter."]},{"chunkId":"chat","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned chat and protocol sections were assessed. Four contract defects block implementation: insertion targets the send/stop control, directional protocol lists are conflated, creation lacks title acquisition, and menu errors lack a reply payload.","findings":[{"id":"chat-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/7/postconditions; /body/dataModelChanges/2; /body/testStrategy","message":"The design repeatedly targets #insrc-prompt for text insertion and focus, but that element is the send/stop button span. The editable textarea is #insrc-input. Implementing the specified handler would leave the submitted input unchanged or corrupt the send control; focusing it also places subsequent keyboard activation on send/stop rather than editing. Correct the contracts, migration instructions, citation c1 and tests to target #insrc-input. Reconcile the cursor-insertion wording with the edge case requiring newline-separated append, and test preservation of existing textarea content plus absence of submit-turn/cancel-turn messages.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:214","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:312","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2783 — #insrc-prompt is a role=button span; the next element is textarea #insrc-input","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2721 — box resolves #insrc-input and doSubmit reads box.value","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2736 — #insrc-prompt activates submit or cancellation","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1946"]},{"id":"chat-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/1; /body/errorPaths/invariantsToPreserve/2; /body/migration; /citations/1; /citations/6","message":"The design explicitly requires every new message in BOTH direction-specific const arrays, despite defining six webview→host and two host→webview messages. The existing protocol treats these arrays as discriminants for their respective directions, and existing tests assert that messages appear only on their own side. Adding all eight to both arrays breaks that contract. Specify six additions to WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES and two to HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES, with matching unions and direction-isolation tests. Also correct the claim that protocol.test.ts already proves complete union/list exhaustiveness: its checks enumerate selected kinds rather than establish full equality.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:234","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:319","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:365 — arrays describe discriminants of each direction","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts — docs-decision-result/docs-companion/open-companion tests assert own-side membership and opposite-side absence","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts:141 — explicitly notes the absence of exhaustive list checking"]},{"id":"chat-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/2; /body/contractDetails/api/5; /body/testStrategy","message":"The New scratchpad action posts a payload-free scratch-new message, but createScratch requires a non-empty title. No host prompt, webview title field, generated default, or cancellation behavior connects these contracts. Consequently the principal creation flow cannot be implemented from the specified interaction without inventing a product decision. Define where the title comes from, its validation/default policy, and cancellation semantics; add an integration test driving New through title acquisition to creation, list refresh and document opening.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:77 — createScratch(title: string, body?: string)","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:94 — title must be non-empty","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:154 — scratch-new has no title payload","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:166","/body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping — creation is tested at store level, without the missing title-acquisition flow"]},{"id":"chat-04","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/5; /body/dataModelChanges/1; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/0","message":"Filesystem failures must produce a 'scratchpads unavailable: <reason>' row in the chat menu, but the only declared list reply is scratch-list {entries}. ScratchEntry contains only file metadata, and no error/status field or separate error message is defined. The host therefore has no contracted way to communicate the required failure state to the chat renderer. Define a typed error representation distinct from a successful empty list, its rendering and recovery behavior, and an integration test covering list/create failure followed by successful retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:154","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:223 — ScratchEntry metadata fields","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:272 — required unavailable menu row","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts — attachments-pending provides an explicit optional error field for the analogous existing flow","/body/testStrategy/testLevels/1"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/6","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2435-2495","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2615-2744","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2776-2806","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3233-3256","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1946-1963","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447-473"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Specify runtime rejection of non-string id/text payloads and whether the 64 KiB limit measures UTF-8 bytes, including ellipsis handling. Cover multibyte selections at the boundary.","Include selection-to-button interaction in integration coverage so clicking the floating button preserves the selected text despite focus and selectionchange events."]},{"chunkId":"panels","status":"incomplete","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected. Panel API integration, document lifecycle, and UX artifact adequacy require correction. Companion sources were inspected, but actual visual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"panels-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/6; /body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4; /body/migration","message":"The specified reuse contract does not match the cited implementation. PanelFactory is a function accepting {viewType, title} and returning PanelHandle, whereas the LLD specifies panels.create(viewType, title): WebviewPanel. The injected factory is scoped inside construction of the existing panel host; shellHtml and openSingleton are private helpers, and that host exposes no scratchpad methods. Consequently the proposed extension/chat wiring cannot access the promised shared lifecycle and shell through the stated API. Define the concrete host/dependency additions or helper extraction, use the actual PanelHandle boundary, and reconcile the never-throw signature with the optional result needed when creation fails. Cover creation failure and lifecycle reuse through that boundary.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:172-193","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:355-359","vscode-plugin/src/panels/types.ts — PanelFactory, PanelHandle and WebviewPanelHost","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447 — factory injected into createWebviewPanelHost","vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:214 — private openSingleton returns PanelHandle | undefined","vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:635 — private shellHtml"]},{"id":"panels-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/6; /body/dataModelChanges/3; /body/errorPaths; /body/testStrategy","message":"A singleton document panel is required, but its document-switching contract is missing. Opening B while A is displayed needs an active document identity, replacement of content/title/selection state, and protection against an earlier asynchronous read completing afterward. Without these rules, a slow A read can replace B, and the unqualified instruction to close the document panel on ScratchNotFound can close B when a stale request for A fails. Define identity and generation checks, disposal invalidation, and deletion matching for the currently displayed id. Add integration cases for A→B switching with reversed read completion, stale ENOENT, deleting a different document, and close/reopen during a read.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:106 — asynchronous readScratch","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:145 — deleting currently open document closes its panel","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:254 — singleton document panel","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:280 — closes document panel if open on ScratchNotFound","/body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping — singleton reuse is covered, document switching and stale reads are not","vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts — existing repoSelectionGeneration/repoRenderGeneration guards illustrate the applicable asynchronous-render convention"]},{"id":"panels-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/edgeCases; /body/migration; /body/testStrategy","message":"The design promises that deleting the file backing an open document from the filesystem closes the panel or shows an empty state, but defines no observation or revalidation mechanism. Its ENOENT handling only runs when readScratch is invoked; an already-rendered document can remain open indefinitely and continue sending deleted content. Specify whether a watcher, focus refresh, or another explicit event detects external deletion, including disposal of that subscription and refresh of the browse table. Alternatively narrow the stated guarantee to the next interaction. Test the chosen behavior.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:278-281 — missing-file detection occurs on read","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:311 — external deletion promises panel closure or empty state","/body/contractDetails — no watcher, focus refresh or document revalidation contract","/body/migration — no external-change observation wiring","/body/testStrategy — no open-document external-deletion test"]},{"id":"panels-04","severity":"MED","location":"/body/uxDefinition; /body/companions; document:line:401","message":"The authored UX definition contains only four TextBlocks, and the generated mock contains four paragraphs repeating those descriptions. It does not depict the browse table, icon controls, popup placement, document selection, or floating button placement, so it cannot substantiate the changed layout and interaction states claimed by the UX companion. Replace the prose-only mock with structured layouts showing these surfaces and the relevant empty/error and selected/unselected states, then regenerate and inspect the companion.","evidenceReferences":["/body/uxDefinition/body/0 through /body/uxDefinition/body/3 — all elements are TextBlock","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ux-mock.html — .ux-card contains four p.ux-text elements, with no depicted product table or action controls","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:179-193 — required table and selection controls","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:270-273 — required unavailable/error states"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/uxDefinition","/body/companions","/citations/2","/citations/5","document:line:261","document:line:401","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447-473","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:724-842","vscode-plugin/src/panels/types.ts","vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts","vscode-plugin/src/panels/__tests__/webview-host.test.ts — lifecycle/CSP test declarations","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts — ChatPanelHost, ChatPanelChannel, dependencies and channel disposal wiring","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/sequence-diagram.html","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/component-dependency.html","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ux-mock.html"],"limitations":["Actual renderings of sequence-diagram.html, component-dependency.html and ux-mock.html under docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ could not be inspected. The headless-rendering attempt failed with a module export error, and the browser access host was unavailable. Their generated HTML, diagram sources and descriptive content were inspected; visual layout and successful diagram rendering remain unverified."],"advice":["Make the sequence diagram show the host's read and document-render delivery before selection becomes possible. Its current trace jumps from scratch-open/scratch-browse to selection handling, leaving the main panel handoff only in descriptive prose.","Include a selection-to-button click integration test that preserves the captured selection across pointer focus and selectionchange events."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reconciled all four completed assessments against the current standalone LLD and canonical artifact. All 39 inventory units have substantive inspection coverage, and live file hashes match the reviewed checkpoint baseline. No additional distinct defect was demonstrated. Existing findings remain applicable; mandatory visual verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/EPIC-4642d49ab0593787.json","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/sequence-diagram.html","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/component-dependency.html","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ux-mock.html","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2780","vscode-plugin/src/panels/types.ts"],"limitations":["Actual renderings of sequence-diagram.html, component-dependency.html and ux-mock.html in docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ remain unverified. The completed panels assessment records failed rendering and browser access attempts. This consistency check inspected generated sources and their alignment with structured definitions, but cannot establish successful rendering or visual layout."],"advice":["Address store-01/store-02, chat-01 through chat-04, and panels-01 through panels-04 as the existing findings; this consistency assessment does not duplicate them.","Propagate contract corrections through narrative, structured definitions, generated companions, migration instructions and proving tests. In particular, the incorrect #insrc-prompt insertion target also appears in the sequence definition and generated diagram.","Retain the standalone scope: no parent HLD or declared SPEC is present. Explicit ac1–ac5 definitions and a statement about in-plugin editing would improve traceability, as already noted by the scope assessment."]}],"progress":{"status":"incomplete","phase":"complete","completedChunks":5,"totalChunks":5,"lastMeaningfulActivityAt":null,"activeToolCount":0,"requiresUserInput":false,"checkpointPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","sequence":0,"reviewElapsedMs":0,"unitElapsedMs":null,"observedAt":"2026-11-13T06:47:49.107Z","freshness":"stored"},"startedAt":"2026-11-13T06:39:00.284Z","reviewer":"daemon","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","unit":{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","executionId":"007b98b7-af94-49eb-8815-f43e4806758a","dispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[]},"plan":{"chunks":[{"id":"scope","title":"Standalone requirements, scope and architectural choice","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","document:line:26"],"concerns":["Establish intended requirements from captured standalone scope and any declared SPEC; do not invent Epic or HLD ancestry.","Assess functional completeness, acceptance criteria, non-goals, unresolved decisions and rationale for the selected approach.","Check repository boundaries, shared responsibilities and the requirement for filesystem storage without daemon IPC."],"dependsOn":[],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"store","title":"Scratch filesystem store and persistence contracts","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","/citations/3","/citations/4"],"concerns":["Inspect store interfaces, metadata semantics, root derivation, identifier validation, file containment, enumeration, ordering and lazy initialization.","Assess creation, naming collisions, atomic writes, cleanup, read/delete behavior and filesystem error handling.","Verify dependency injection, ownership of files, compatibility, implementation order and meaningful unit-test coverage against cited store and path code.","Assess all assigned shared sections, focusing on persistence obligations and their integration dependencies."],"dependsOn":["scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"chat","title":"Chat protocol, menu and input insertion","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/6"],"concerns":["Inspect message direction, payload types, runtime handling and protocol exhaustiveness against actual protocol and chat code.","Trace scratchpad button, recent/new/browse menu actions and host replies through creation and input insertion.","Check title acquisition, selection truncation, cursor/append semantics, focus, unsent-input preservation and the never-auto-send requirement.","Assess failures, stale state, existing attachment behavior and integration-test coverage.","Assess all assigned shared sections for chat and protocol obligations."],"dependsOn":["scope","store"],"purpose":"substantive