migration sequence.","Confirm complete inventory coverage and distinguish demonstrated defects, mandatory inspection limitations and optional advice."],"dependsOn":["scope","store","chat","panels"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"Every inventory unit maps to a substantive chunk. Shared contract, model, error, test and migration sections are intentionally assigned across store, chat and panel responsibilities so each reviewer retains interfaces, logic, failure handling and coverage together. Scope precedes persistence, protocol integration and panel orchestration. The final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk and supplements their coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["store","chat","panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["store","chat","panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["store","chat","panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["store","chat","panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["store","chat","panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/uxDefinition","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","chunkIds":["store"]},{"unitId":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","chunkIds":["chat"]},{"unitId":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","chunkIds":["chat"]},{"unitId":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","chunkIds":["store"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["chat"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["chat"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["store"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["store"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["chat"]},{"unitId":"document:line:26","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:261","chunkIds":["panels"]},{"unitId":"document:line:401","chunkIds":["panels"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"store","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"chat","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"panels","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":2,"MED":8,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The selected a1 approach covers the captured standalone scope: recent/new/browse navigation, a tabular editor pane, selection-to-chat insertion without auto-send, and plain filesystem storage without daemon IPC. No parent HLD or SPEC is declared. Extension ownership and reuse of existing file-store patterns are consistent with the repository boundaries. No blocking defect was demonstrated in the assigned scope sections.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","document:line:26","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:1-95","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447-478","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:631-640","src/shared/paths.ts:1-8","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:340-348"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define ac1–ac5 explicitly alongside the captured scope; the acceptance mapping currently identifies them only through their proving tests.","State whether editing existing scratchpad content inside the plugin is outside this increment. The selected approach specifies a document reader and create/read/delete storage operations."]},{"chunkId":"store","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The persistence design covers lazy initialization, filesystem errors, enumeration and test seams, but its identifier validation permits directory targets and its creation protocol lacks collision-safe publication across writers.","findings":[{"id":"store-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/contractDetails/api — readScratch/deleteScratch; /body/dataModelChanges/0","message":"The prescribed ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ validator accepts both '.' and '..'. Joining these ids to the store root targets the scratches directory itself or its ~/.insrc parent, violating the plain-scratchpad-file boundary. This is especially dangerous because the referenced attachment-store adapter implements rm with recursive:true. Require a scratchpad filename, explicitly reject dot segments, enforce containment and file-only deletion, and test that invalid ids cause no filesystem calls. Specify handling of symlinks so reads cannot follow a scratch entry outside the root.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:115","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:137","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:223","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:61","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:95","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/attachment-store.test.ts — remove rejects '.' and '..'","Read-only Node evaluation confirmed the specified regex accepts '..' and path.join('/home/u/.insrc/scratches', '..') resolves to '/home/u/.insrc'."]},{"id":"store-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api — createScratch; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases","message":"The design combines second-resolution names, a suffix collision ladder and temp-file-plus-rename publication without defining exclusive destination reservation or coordination. Two creates for the same title, including creates from separate VS Code windows sharing PATHS.insrc, can choose the same available basename; ordinary rename can replace the first completed scratchpad with the second. Define unique temporary names and a publication mechanism that cannot overwrite an existing destination, with collision retries covering independent store instances. Include an interleaved concurrent-create test proving both contents survive.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:98","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:99","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:304","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:330","src/shared/paths.ts:4","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts:125"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","/citations/3","/citations/4","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/attachment-store.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fake-attachment-fs.ts","src/shared/paths.ts","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:628"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define ScratchEntry field types and derivation explicitly: name after restart, mtime units, byte-size semantics and deterministic ordering when modification times tie.","Align ScratchStoreDeps with the activation example: the contract requires fs, while migration wiring omits it. The referenced attachment store makes fs optional and defaults to its Node adapter."]},{"chunkId":"chat","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned chat and protocol sections were assessed. Four contract defects block implementation: insertion targets the send/stop control, directional protocol lists are conflated, creation lacks title acquisition, and menu errors lack a reply payload.","findings":[{"id":"chat-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/7/postconditions; /body/dataModelChanges/2; /body/testStrategy","message":"The design repeatedly targets #insrc-prompt for text insertion and focus, but that element is the send/stop button span. The editable textarea is #insrc-input. Implementing the specified handler would leave the submitted input unchanged or corrupt the send control; focusing it also places subsequent keyboard activation on send/stop rather than editing. Correct the contracts, migration instructions, citation c1 and tests to target #insrc-input. Reconcile the cursor-insertion wording with the edge case requiring newline-separated append, and test preservation of existing textarea content plus absence of submit-turn/cancel-turn messages.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:214","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:312","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2783 — #insrc-prompt is a role=button span; the next element is textarea #insrc-input","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2721 — box resolves #insrc-input and doSubmit reads box.value","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2736 — #insrc-prompt activates submit or cancellation","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1946"]},{"id":"chat-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/1; /body/errorPaths/invariantsToPreserve/2; /body/migration; /citations/1; /citations/6","message":"The design explicitly requires every new message in BOTH direction-specific const arrays, despite defining six webview→host and two host→webview messages. The existing protocol treats these arrays as discriminants for their respective directions, and existing tests assert that messages appear only on their own side. Adding all eight to both arrays breaks that contract. Specify six additions to WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES and two to HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES, with matching unions and direction-isolation tests. Also correct the claim that protocol.test.ts already proves complete union/list exhaustiveness: its checks enumerate selected kinds rather than establish full equality.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:234","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:319","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:365 — arrays describe discriminants of each direction","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts — docs-decision-result/docs-companion/open-companion tests assert own-side membership and opposite-side absence","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts:141 — explicitly notes the absence of exhaustive list checking"]},{"id":"chat-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/2; /body/contractDetails/api/5; /body/testStrategy","message":"The New scratchpad action posts a payload-free scratch-new message, but createScratch requires a non-empty title. No host prompt, webview title field, generated default, or cancellation behavior connects these contracts. Consequently the principal creation flow cannot be implemented from the specified interaction without inventing a product decision. Define where the title comes from, its validation/default policy, and cancellation semantics; add an integration test driving New through title acquisition to creation, list refresh and document opening.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:77 — createScratch(title: string, body?: string)","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:94 — title must be non-empty","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:154 — scratch-new has no title payload","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:166","/body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping — creation is tested at store level, without the missing title-acquisition flow"]},{"id":"chat-04","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/5; /body/dataModelChanges/1; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/0","message":"Filesystem failures must produce a 'scratchpads unavailable: <reason>' row in the chat menu, but the only declared list reply is scratch-list {entries}. ScratchEntry contains only file metadata, and no error/status field or separate error message is defined. The host therefore has no contracted way to communicate the required failure state to the chat renderer. Define a typed error representation distinct from a successful empty list, its rendering and recovery behavior, and an integration test covering list/create failure followed by successful retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:154","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:223 — ScratchEntry metadata fields","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:272 — required unavailable menu row","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts — attachments-pending provides an explicit optional error field for the analogous existing flow","/body/testStrategy/testLevels/1"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/6","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2435-2495","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2615-2744","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2776-2806","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3233-3256","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1946-1963","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447-473"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Specify runtime rejection of non-string id/text payloads and whether the 64 KiB limit measures UTF-8 bytes, including ellipsis handling. Cover multibyte selections at the boundary.","Include selection-to-button interaction in integration coverage so clicking the floating button preserves the selected text despite focus and selectionchange events."]},{"chunkId":"panels","status":"incomplete","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected. Panel API integration, document lifecycle, and UX artifact adequacy require correction. Companion sources were inspected, but actual visual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"panels-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/6; /body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4; /body/migration","message":"The specified reuse contract does not match the cited implementation. PanelFactory is a function accepting {viewType, title} and returning PanelHandle, whereas the LLD specifies panels.create(viewType, title): WebviewPanel. The injected factory is scoped inside construction of the existing panel host; shellHtml and openSingleton are private helpers, and that host exposes no scratchpad methods. Consequently the proposed extension/chat wiring cannot access the promised shared lifecycle and shell through the stated API. Define the concrete host/dependency additions or helper extraction, use the actual PanelHandle boundary, and reconcile the never-throw signature with the optional result needed when creation fails. Cover creation failure and lifecycle reuse through that boundary.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:172-193","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:355-359","vscode-plugin/src/panels/types.ts — PanelFactory, PanelHandle and WebviewPanelHost","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447 — factory injected into createWebviewPanelHost","vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:214 — private openSingleton returns PanelHandle | undefined","vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts:635 — private shellHtml"]},{"id":"panels-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/6; /body/dataModelChanges/3; /body/errorPaths; /body/testStrategy","message":"A singleton document panel is required, but its document-switching contract is missing. Opening B while A is displayed needs an active document identity, replacement of content/title/selection state, and protection against an earlier asynchronous read completing afterward. Without these rules, a slow A read can replace B, and the unqualified instruction to close the document panel on ScratchNotFound can close B when a stale request for A fails. Define identity and generation checks, disposal invalidation, and deletion matching for the currently displayed id. Add integration cases for A→B switching with reversed read completion, stale ENOENT, deleting a different document, and close/reopen during a read.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:106 — asynchronous readScratch","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:145 — deleting currently open document closes its panel","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:254 — singleton document panel","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:280 — closes document panel if open on ScratchNotFound","/body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping — singleton reuse is covered, document switching and stale reads are not","vscode-plugin/src/panels/webview-host.ts — existing repoSelectionGeneration/repoRenderGeneration guards illustrate the applicable asynchronous-render convention"]},{"id":"panels-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/edgeCases; /body/migration; /body/testStrategy","message":"The design promises that deleting the file backing an open document from the filesystem closes the panel or shows an empty state, but defines no observation or revalidation mechanism. Its ENOENT handling only runs when readScratch is invoked; an already-rendered document can remain open indefinitely and continue sending deleted content. Specify whether a watcher, focus refresh, or another explicit event detects external deletion, including disposal of that subscription and refresh of the browse table. Alternatively narrow the stated guarantee to the next interaction. Test the chosen behavior.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:278-281 — missing-file detection occurs on read","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:311 — external deletion promises panel closure or empty state","/body/contractDetails — no watcher, focus refresh or document revalidation contract","/body/migration — no external-change observation wiring","/body/testStrategy — no open-document external-deletion test"]},{"id":"panels-04","severity":"MED","location":"/body/uxDefinition; /body/companions; document:line:401","message":"The authored UX definition contains only four TextBlocks, and the generated mock contains four paragraphs repeating those descriptions. It does not depict the browse table, icon controls, popup placement, document selection, or floating button placement, so it cannot substantiate the changed layout and interaction states claimed by the UX companion. Replace the prose-only mock with structured layouts showing these surfaces and the relevant empty/error and selected/unselected states, then regenerate and inspect the companion.","evidenceReferences":["/body/uxDefinition/body/0 through /body/uxDefinition/body/3 — all elements are TextBlock","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/ux-mock.html — .ux-card contains four p.ux-text elements, with no depicted product table or action controls","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:179-193 — required table and selection controls","docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md:270-273 — required unavailable/error states"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/componentDependencyDefinition","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/uxDefinition","/body/companions","/citations/2","/citations/5","document:line:261","document:line:401","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/vs-code-plugin-scratchpads-insrc-scratches-E202611134642d49a/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-4642d49ab0593787-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/lld-4642d49ab0593787-s1-r1.json","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:447-473","vscode-plugin/src/exten